  "deviations": [
    "E2/E4/E6 use a numpy twin of the champion's SAMPLED path at full width: no structural pruning (active-set narrowing) and no terminal-three-layer fold algebra. Both omissions are conservative for error magnitude (pruning narrows the products; the fold is an exact re-association of the same float32 maps). The twin's depth-1 injected MSE was cross-checked against the SHIPPED RowBlockedBatchedWinograd kernel and agrees to 5.5% (e6).",
    "E2 arms compare against a float64-classical reference, not against benchmark truth (firewall forbids truth reads). The MSE translation therefore uses the rigorous triangle-inequality worst case r_MSE <= (1+sqrt(mean(delta^2)/MSE_raw))^2, which needs no truth.",
    "Haar rotation omitted in the 4-net E2 sweep (W0 iid Gaussian is rotation-invariant in distribution); it IS applied in the 6-seed bias decomposition, which is where it matters.",
    "MLP weights are generated with numpy default_rng at the same He scale as whestbench.generation.sample_mlp rather than through the flopscope RNG; distribution identical, streams differ.",
    "Cost-side figures (r(d), 57.4164% eligibility, 1.2118x) are U-F1's own and were NOT independently metered here; only the MSE side is mine."
  ],
